IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bkv-law`
IMPORT `bkv-ifg-law`

-- Seat layer, second layer for the requester: a person who asks a federal authority for a document about the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases.
-- bkv-seat.l4 asks whether another ground for refusing access applies as one fact. This layer asks each ground of IFG §§ 3 to 6 separately, and answers the same question, under both readings of § 9(5) BKV.
-- It builds the law layers' records internally from plain inputs and calls their rules: `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` (bkv-law.l4) with the field
-- `another ground for refusing access applies` set from `a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` (bkv-ifg-law.l4). It restates no rule. It defines names that bkv-seat.l4 does not. Target compiler: main.
-- Every ground input is a fact the requester can state or a judgment asked as an input, and each @desc says which (NOTES.md, forks F6 to F13). Several inputs are about the authority's view, not yours; answer them as you expect it to decide.
-- The first five inputs are the same as in bkv-seat.l4; the rest are the grounds. A ground that cannot apply to your request is simply false.
-- The facts describe the information you ask for: if you ask only for a part of a document, answer about that part, as the text says 'soweit' (NOTES.md, fork F12).

-- The grounds are many, so a form should ask only the ones the answer still depends on: any ground that is true settles the answer, and every ground must be false for access to stand.
§ `Can I get the document? Each ground for refusal spelled out`

@export Am I entitled to access to this document of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases under the Freedom of Information Act, with every ground for refusal in §§ 3 to 6 IFG spelled out, reading § 9(5) BKV as it has stood since 1 August 2026? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    -- the document and the request
    `federal request`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another duty attaches`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 1
    `harm to international relations`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect Germany's international relations (§ 3 no. 1 a IFG); false if not.
    `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Federal Armed Forces (§ 3 no. 1 b IFG); false if not.
    `harm to internal or external security`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect interests of internal or external security (§ 3 no. 1 c IFG); false if not.
    `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities (§ 3 no. 1 d IFG); false if not.
    `harm to external financial control`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect matters of external financial control (§ 3 no. 1 e IFG); false if not.
    `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade and payments (§ 3 no. 1 f IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a pending court case`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a fair trial`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect a person's claim to a fair trial (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to an investigation`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 2
    `danger to public safety`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could endanger public safety (§ 3 no. 2 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 3
    `impairs confidential international negotiations`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations (§ 3 no. 3 a IFG); false if not.
    `impairs the deliberations of an authority`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of an authority's deliberations (§ 3 no. 3 b IFG); false if not. Whether a paper that is only a basis for the authority's deliberations and shows nothing of how it formed its view is protected at all was left open in BVerwG 7 C 4.11, para. 32.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty
    `classified as a Verschlusssache`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is classified as a Verschlusssache under the general administrative rule on the protection of classified information (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `professional secret`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a professional secret (Berufsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `special official secret`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a special official secret (besonderes Amtsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 5
    `comes from another public body`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information comes from another public body (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if the authority made it.
    `drawn in only temporarily`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority drew the information in only temporarily (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if not.
    `not meant to join its own records`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is not meant to become part of the authority's own records (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if it is.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 6
    `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the economic interests of the social insurance funds (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 7
    `received in confidence`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information was collected or transmitted in confidence (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if it was submitted as non-confidential.
    `third party still wants confidence`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, on the day you made the request, the third party who gave the information still had an interest in its being treated as confidential (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if that interest has ended.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 8
    `asking an intelligence service`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask is an intelligence service (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    `asking about security-clearance tasks`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask performs tasks within § 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act (Sicherheitsüberprüfungsgesetz) and your request concerns those tasks (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 4(1)
    `a draft of a decision`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a draft of a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `work immediately preparing a decision`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party, such as an association's written statement (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `such a paper still prepares a decision`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual, so that evidence, an expert opinion or a third party's statement does serve the immediate preparation of a decision (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG says they regularly do not); false in the usual case.
    `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known before the decision is taken would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case, access should still be granted`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that the application should not be refused although § 4(1) IFG would otherwise apply (the provision says it 'should' be refused); false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 5
    `personal data of a third party`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains personal data of a person other than you (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `special category personal data`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation, such as health data (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the third party consented`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person whose data it is has consented to your getting access (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `the consent was express`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that consent was given expressly (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if there was no consent or it was not express.
    `my interest outweighs the third party interest`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if, weighing your interest in the information against the third party's interest worthy of protection in excluding access, yours outweighs theirs (§ 5(1) sentence 1 IFG). This is a judgment for the authority and then a court: answer it as you expect it to be decided.
    `data from service, office or mandate files`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data come from documents that relate to the third party's service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `personal data under a professional or official secret`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `only name, title and office contact details`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number (§ 5(3) IFG); false if they go further.
    `the third party gave an expert opinion`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way (§ 5(3) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case for section 5(3)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that § 5(3) IFG, which says the interest of the requester outweighs 'in der Regel' (as a rule) in the situation it describes, does not settle the weighing here; false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 6
    `copyright or other intellectual property`                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains copyright-protected material or other intellectual property (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not.
    `that protection stands in the way`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access you ask for (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not, for example because the holder of the right agrees.
    `a trade or business secret`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains a trade or business secret (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the holder of the secret consented`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person concerned, the one whose secret it is, has consented to your getting access to it (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I entitled to access with the grounds for refusal spelled out and section 9(5) BKV as in force` MEANS
    `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` `as in force from 1 August 2026` request
    WHERE
        `the facts about section 3 no. 1` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 1` WITH
            `disclosure could adversely affect international relations` IS `harm to international relations`
            `disclosure could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Bundeswehr` IS `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`
            `disclosure could adversely affect interests of internal or external security` IS `harm to internal or external security`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities` IS `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`
            `disclosure could adversely affect matters of external financial control` IS `harm to external financial control`
            `disclosure could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade` IS `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case` IS `harm to a pending court case`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the claim of a person to a fair trial` IS `harm to a fair trial`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations` IS `harm to an investigation`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 2` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 2` WITH
            `disclosure could endanger public safety` IS `danger to public safety`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 3` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 3` WITH
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations` IS `impairs confidential international negotiations`
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of the deliberations of an authority` IS `impairs the deliberations of an authority`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` WITH
            `the information is subject to a duty of secrecy set by the general administrative rule on classified information` IS `classified as a Verschlusssache`
            `the information is subject to a professional secret` IS `professional secret`
            `the information is subject to a special official secret` IS `special official secret`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 5` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 5` WITH
            `the information comes from another public body` IS `comes from another public body`
            `the information was drawn in only temporarily` IS `drawn in only temporarily`
            `the information is not meant to become part of the own records of the authority` IS `not meant to join its own records`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 6` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 6` WITH
            `disclosure is apt to impair fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce` IS `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`
            `disclosure is apt to impair economic interests of the social insurance funds` IS `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 7` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 7` WITH
            `the information was collected or transmitted in confidence` IS `received in confidence`
            `the interest of the third party in confidential treatment still persists at the time of the request` IS `third party still wants confidence`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 8` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 8` WITH
            `the authority asked is an intelligence service` IS `asking an intelligence service`
            `the authority asked performs tasks within section 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act and the information concerns them` IS `asking about security-clearance tasks`
        `the facts about section 4(1)` MEANS `Facts about section 4(1)` WITH
            `the information is a draft of a decision` IS `a draft of a decision`
            `the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision` IS `work immediately preparing a decision`
            `the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party` IS `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`
            `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves the immediate preparation of a decision` IS `such a paper still prepares a decision`
            `premature disclosure would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures` IS `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`
            `the case is atypical, so that the application should not be refused` IS `atypical case, access should still be granted`
        `the facts about section 5` MEANS `Facts about section 5` WITH
            `the information contains personal data of a third party` IS `personal data of a third party`
            `the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation` IS `special category personal data`
            `the third party has consented to access` IS `the third party consented`
            `the consent of the third party was express` IS `the consent was express`
            `the interest of the requester in the information outweighs the interest of the third party in excluding access` IS `my interest outweighs the third party interest`
            `the personal data come from documents about the service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party` IS `data from service, office or mandate files`
            `the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret` IS `personal data under a professional or official secret`
            `the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number` IS `only name, title and office contact details`
            `the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way` IS `the third party gave an expert opinion`
            `the case is atypical, so that section 5(3) does not settle the weighing` IS `atypical case for section 5(3)`
        `the facts about section 6` MEANS `Facts about section 6` WITH
            `the information contains intellectual property` IS `copyright or other intellectual property`
            `the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access requested` IS `that protection stands in the way`
            `the information contains a trade or business secret` IS `a trade or business secret`
            `the person concerned has consented to access to the trade or business secret` IS `the holder of the secret consented`
        grounds MEANS `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access` WITH
            `facts for section 3 no. 1` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 1`
            `facts for section 3 no. 2` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 2`
            `facts for section 3 no. 3` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 3`
            `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty`
            `facts for section 3 no. 5` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 5`
            `facts for section 3 no. 6` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 6`
            `facts for section 3 no. 7` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 7`
            `facts for section 3 no. 8` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 8`
            `facts for section 4(1)` IS `the facts about section 4(1)`
            `facts for section 5` IS `the facts about section 5`
            `facts for section 6` IS `the facts about section 6`
        request MEANS `Request for a document` WITH
            `is addressed to a federal authority and asks for official information` IS `federal request`
            `the document was prepared outside the Council and the Ministry` IS `prepared outside`
            `the document was submitted to the Council for its deliberations` IS `submitted to the Council`
            `the document is a recommendation an opinion or a closing report of the Council` IS `recommendation or report`
            `another ground for refusing access applies` IS (`a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` grounds)
            `another statutory confidentiality duty attaches to the document` IS `another duty attaches`

-- The next group only arises if the document is an external paper submitted to the Council, the kind the 2026 amendment brought under § 9(5).
-- A form can ask "Was it written outside the Council?" before showing it.
§ `What if the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV is void?`

@export Am I entitled to access to this document of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases under the Freedom of Information Act, with every ground for refusal in §§ 3 to 6 IFG spelled out, if the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 9(1a) sentence 4 of Book VII of the Social Code? Answers yes or no.
GIVEN
    -- the document and the request
    `federal request`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another duty attaches`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 1
    `harm to international relations`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect Germany's international relations (§ 3 no. 1 a IFG); false if not.
    `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Federal Armed Forces (§ 3 no. 1 b IFG); false if not.
    `harm to internal or external security`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect interests of internal or external security (§ 3 no. 1 c IFG); false if not.
    `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities (§ 3 no. 1 d IFG); false if not.
    `harm to external financial control`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect matters of external financial control (§ 3 no. 1 e IFG); false if not.
    `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade and payments (§ 3 no. 1 f IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a pending court case`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a fair trial`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect a person's claim to a fair trial (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to an investigation`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 2
    `danger to public safety`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could endanger public safety (§ 3 no. 2 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 3
    `impairs confidential international negotiations`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations (§ 3 no. 3 a IFG); false if not.
    `impairs the deliberations of an authority`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of an authority's deliberations (§ 3 no. 3 b IFG); false if not. Whether a paper that is only a basis for the authority's deliberations and shows nothing of how it formed its view is protected at all was left open in BVerwG 7 C 4.11, para. 32.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty
    `classified as a Verschlusssache`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is classified as a Verschlusssache under the general administrative rule on the protection of classified information (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `professional secret`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a professional secret (Berufsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `special official secret`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a special official secret (besonderes Amtsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 5
    `comes from another public body`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information comes from another public body (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if the authority made it.
    `drawn in only temporarily`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority drew the information in only temporarily (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if not.
    `not meant to join its own records`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is not meant to become part of the authority's own records (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if it is.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 6
    `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the economic interests of the social insurance funds (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 7
    `received in confidence`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information was collected or transmitted in confidence (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if it was submitted as non-confidential.
    `third party still wants confidence`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, on the day you made the request, the third party who gave the information still had an interest in its being treated as confidential (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if that interest has ended.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 8
    `asking an intelligence service`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask is an intelligence service (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    `asking about security-clearance tasks`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask performs tasks within § 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act (Sicherheitsüberprüfungsgesetz) and your request concerns those tasks (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 4(1)
    `a draft of a decision`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a draft of a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `work immediately preparing a decision`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party, such as an association's written statement (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `such a paper still prepares a decision`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual, so that evidence, an expert opinion or a third party's statement does serve the immediate preparation of a decision (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG says they regularly do not); false in the usual case.
    `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known before the decision is taken would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case, access should still be granted`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that the application should not be refused although § 4(1) IFG would otherwise apply (the provision says it 'should' be refused); false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 5
    `personal data of a third party`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains personal data of a person other than you (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `special category personal data`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation, such as health data (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the third party consented`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person whose data it is has consented to your getting access (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `the consent was express`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that consent was given expressly (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if there was no consent or it was not express.
    `my interest outweighs the third party interest`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if, weighing your interest in the information against the third party's interest worthy of protection in excluding access, yours outweighs theirs (§ 5(1) sentence 1 IFG). This is a judgment for the authority and then a court: answer it as you expect it to be decided.
    `data from service, office or mandate files`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data come from documents that relate to the third party's service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `personal data under a professional or official secret`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `only name, title and office contact details`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number (§ 5(3) IFG); false if they go further.
    `the third party gave an expert opinion`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way (§ 5(3) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case for section 5(3)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that § 5(3) IFG, which says the interest of the requester outweighs 'in der Regel' (as a rule) in the situation it describes, does not settle the weighing here; false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 6
    `copyright or other intellectual property`                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains copyright-protected material or other intellectual property (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not.
    `that protection stands in the way`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access you ask for (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not, for example because the holder of the right agrees.
    `a trade or business secret`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains a trade or business secret (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the holder of the secret consented`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person concerned, the one whose secret it is, has consented to your getting access to it (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    -- the citation requirement
    `an exception applies`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV stands; false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I entitled to access with the grounds for refusal spelled out if the 2026 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the requester is entitled to access under the reading` (`the reading of section 9(5) BKV to apply` `an exception applies`) request
    WHERE
        `the facts about section 3 no. 1` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 1` WITH
            `disclosure could adversely affect international relations` IS `harm to international relations`
            `disclosure could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Bundeswehr` IS `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`
            `disclosure could adversely affect interests of internal or external security` IS `harm to internal or external security`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities` IS `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`
            `disclosure could adversely affect matters of external financial control` IS `harm to external financial control`
            `disclosure could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade` IS `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case` IS `harm to a pending court case`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the claim of a person to a fair trial` IS `harm to a fair trial`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations` IS `harm to an investigation`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 2` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 2` WITH
            `disclosure could endanger public safety` IS `danger to public safety`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 3` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 3` WITH
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations` IS `impairs confidential international negotiations`
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of the deliberations of an authority` IS `impairs the deliberations of an authority`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` WITH
            `the information is subject to a duty of secrecy set by the general administrative rule on classified information` IS `classified as a Verschlusssache`
            `the information is subject to a professional secret` IS `professional secret`
            `the information is subject to a special official secret` IS `special official secret`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 5` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 5` WITH
            `the information comes from another public body` IS `comes from another public body`
            `the information was drawn in only temporarily` IS `drawn in only temporarily`
            `the information is not meant to become part of the own records of the authority` IS `not meant to join its own records`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 6` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 6` WITH
            `disclosure is apt to impair fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce` IS `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`
            `disclosure is apt to impair economic interests of the social insurance funds` IS `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 7` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 7` WITH
            `the information was collected or transmitted in confidence` IS `received in confidence`
            `the interest of the third party in confidential treatment still persists at the time of the request` IS `third party still wants confidence`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 8` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 8` WITH
            `the authority asked is an intelligence service` IS `asking an intelligence service`
            `the authority asked performs tasks within section 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act and the information concerns them` IS `asking about security-clearance tasks`
        `the facts about section 4(1)` MEANS `Facts about section 4(1)` WITH
            `the information is a draft of a decision` IS `a draft of a decision`
            `the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision` IS `work immediately preparing a decision`
            `the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party` IS `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`
            `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves the immediate preparation of a decision` IS `such a paper still prepares a decision`
            `premature disclosure would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures` IS `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`
            `the case is atypical, so that the application should not be refused` IS `atypical case, access should still be granted`
        `the facts about section 5` MEANS `Facts about section 5` WITH
            `the information contains personal data of a third party` IS `personal data of a third party`
            `the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation` IS `special category personal data`
            `the third party has consented to access` IS `the third party consented`
            `the consent of the third party was express` IS `the consent was express`
            `the interest of the requester in the information outweighs the interest of the third party in excluding access` IS `my interest outweighs the third party interest`
            `the personal data come from documents about the service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party` IS `data from service, office or mandate files`
            `the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret` IS `personal data under a professional or official secret`
            `the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number` IS `only name, title and office contact details`
            `the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way` IS `the third party gave an expert opinion`
            `the case is atypical, so that section 5(3) does not settle the weighing` IS `atypical case for section 5(3)`
        `the facts about section 6` MEANS `Facts about section 6` WITH
            `the information contains intellectual property` IS `copyright or other intellectual property`
            `the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access requested` IS `that protection stands in the way`
            `the information contains a trade or business secret` IS `a trade or business secret`
            `the person concerned has consented to access to the trade or business secret` IS `the holder of the secret consented`
        grounds MEANS `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access` WITH
            `facts for section 3 no. 1` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 1`
            `facts for section 3 no. 2` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 2`
            `facts for section 3 no. 3` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 3`
            `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty`
            `facts for section 3 no. 5` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 5`
            `facts for section 3 no. 6` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 6`
            `facts for section 3 no. 7` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 7`
            `facts for section 3 no. 8` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 8`
            `facts for section 4(1)` IS `the facts about section 4(1)`
            `facts for section 5` IS `the facts about section 5`
            `facts for section 6` IS `the facts about section 6`
        request MEANS `Request for a document` WITH
            `is addressed to a federal authority and asks for official information` IS `federal request`
            `the document was prepared outside the Council and the Ministry` IS `prepared outside`
            `the document was submitted to the Council for its deliberations` IS `submitted to the Council`
            `the document is a recommendation an opinion or a closing report of the Council` IS `recommendation or report`
            `another ground for refusing access applies` IS (`a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` grounds)
            `another statutory confidentiality duty attaches to the document` IS `another duty attaches`

§ `Which grounds for refusing access apply?`

@export Which grounds for refusing access under §§ 3 to 6 of the Freedom of Information Act apply to this request for a document of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases, reading § 9(5) BKV as it has stood since 1 August 2026? Answers with a list of the grounds that apply; an empty list means none does.
GIVEN
    -- the document and the request
    `federal request`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another duty attaches`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 1
    `harm to international relations`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect Germany's international relations (§ 3 no. 1 a IFG); false if not.
    `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Federal Armed Forces (§ 3 no. 1 b IFG); false if not.
    `harm to internal or external security`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect interests of internal or external security (§ 3 no. 1 c IFG); false if not.
    `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities (§ 3 no. 1 d IFG); false if not.
    `harm to external financial control`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect matters of external financial control (§ 3 no. 1 e IFG); false if not.
    `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade and payments (§ 3 no. 1 f IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a pending court case`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a fair trial`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect a person's claim to a fair trial (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to an investigation`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 2
    `danger to public safety`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could endanger public safety (§ 3 no. 2 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 3
    `impairs confidential international negotiations`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations (§ 3 no. 3 a IFG); false if not.
    `impairs the deliberations of an authority`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of an authority's deliberations (§ 3 no. 3 b IFG); false if not. Whether a paper that is only a basis for the authority's deliberations and shows nothing of how it formed its view is protected at all was left open in BVerwG 7 C 4.11, para. 32.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty
    `classified as a Verschlusssache`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is classified as a Verschlusssache under the general administrative rule on the protection of classified information (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `professional secret`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a professional secret (Berufsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `special official secret`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a special official secret (besonderes Amtsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 5
    `comes from another public body`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information comes from another public body (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if the authority made it.
    `drawn in only temporarily`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority drew the information in only temporarily (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if not.
    `not meant to join its own records`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is not meant to become part of the authority's own records (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if it is.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 6
    `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the economic interests of the social insurance funds (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 7
    `received in confidence`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information was collected or transmitted in confidence (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if it was submitted as non-confidential.
    `third party still wants confidence`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, on the day you made the request, the third party who gave the information still had an interest in its being treated as confidential (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if that interest has ended.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 8
    `asking an intelligence service`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask is an intelligence service (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    `asking about security-clearance tasks`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask performs tasks within § 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act (Sicherheitsüberprüfungsgesetz) and your request concerns those tasks (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 4(1)
    `a draft of a decision`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a draft of a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `work immediately preparing a decision`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party, such as an association's written statement (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `such a paper still prepares a decision`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual, so that evidence, an expert opinion or a third party's statement does serve the immediate preparation of a decision (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG says they regularly do not); false in the usual case.
    `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known before the decision is taken would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case, access should still be granted`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that the application should not be refused although § 4(1) IFG would otherwise apply (the provision says it 'should' be refused); false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 5
    `personal data of a third party`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains personal data of a person other than you (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `special category personal data`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation, such as health data (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the third party consented`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person whose data it is has consented to your getting access (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `the consent was express`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that consent was given expressly (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if there was no consent or it was not express.
    `my interest outweighs the third party interest`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if, weighing your interest in the information against the third party's interest worthy of protection in excluding access, yours outweighs theirs (§ 5(1) sentence 1 IFG). This is a judgment for the authority and then a court: answer it as you expect it to be decided.
    `data from service, office or mandate files`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data come from documents that relate to the third party's service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `personal data under a professional or official secret`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `only name, title and office contact details`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number (§ 5(3) IFG); false if they go further.
    `the third party gave an expert opinion`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way (§ 5(3) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case for section 5(3)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that § 5(3) IFG, which says the interest of the requester outweighs 'in der Regel' (as a rule) in the situation it describes, does not settle the weighing here; false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 6
    `copyright or other intellectual property`                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains copyright-protected material or other intellectual property (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not.
    `that protection stands in the way`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access you ask for (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not, for example because the holder of the right agrees.
    `a trade or business secret`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains a trade or business secret (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the holder of the secret consented`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person concerned, the one whose secret it is, has consented to your getting access to it (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
GIVETH A LIST OF `Ground for refusing access`
`which grounds for refusing access apply with section 9(5) BKV as in force` MEANS
    `the grounds for refusing access that apply` `as in force from 1 August 2026` request grounds
    WHERE
        `the facts about section 3 no. 1` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 1` WITH
            `disclosure could adversely affect international relations` IS `harm to international relations`
            `disclosure could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Bundeswehr` IS `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`
            `disclosure could adversely affect interests of internal or external security` IS `harm to internal or external security`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities` IS `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`
            `disclosure could adversely affect matters of external financial control` IS `harm to external financial control`
            `disclosure could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade` IS `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case` IS `harm to a pending court case`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the claim of a person to a fair trial` IS `harm to a fair trial`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations` IS `harm to an investigation`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 2` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 2` WITH
            `disclosure could endanger public safety` IS `danger to public safety`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 3` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 3` WITH
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations` IS `impairs confidential international negotiations`
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of the deliberations of an authority` IS `impairs the deliberations of an authority`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` WITH
            `the information is subject to a duty of secrecy set by the general administrative rule on classified information` IS `classified as a Verschlusssache`
            `the information is subject to a professional secret` IS `professional secret`
            `the information is subject to a special official secret` IS `special official secret`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 5` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 5` WITH
            `the information comes from another public body` IS `comes from another public body`
            `the information was drawn in only temporarily` IS `drawn in only temporarily`
            `the information is not meant to become part of the own records of the authority` IS `not meant to join its own records`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 6` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 6` WITH
            `disclosure is apt to impair fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce` IS `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`
            `disclosure is apt to impair economic interests of the social insurance funds` IS `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 7` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 7` WITH
            `the information was collected or transmitted in confidence` IS `received in confidence`
            `the interest of the third party in confidential treatment still persists at the time of the request` IS `third party still wants confidence`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 8` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 8` WITH
            `the authority asked is an intelligence service` IS `asking an intelligence service`
            `the authority asked performs tasks within section 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act and the information concerns them` IS `asking about security-clearance tasks`
        `the facts about section 4(1)` MEANS `Facts about section 4(1)` WITH
            `the information is a draft of a decision` IS `a draft of a decision`
            `the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision` IS `work immediately preparing a decision`
            `the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party` IS `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`
            `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves the immediate preparation of a decision` IS `such a paper still prepares a decision`
            `premature disclosure would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures` IS `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`
            `the case is atypical, so that the application should not be refused` IS `atypical case, access should still be granted`
        `the facts about section 5` MEANS `Facts about section 5` WITH
            `the information contains personal data of a third party` IS `personal data of a third party`
            `the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation` IS `special category personal data`
            `the third party has consented to access` IS `the third party consented`
            `the consent of the third party was express` IS `the consent was express`
            `the interest of the requester in the information outweighs the interest of the third party in excluding access` IS `my interest outweighs the third party interest`
            `the personal data come from documents about the service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party` IS `data from service, office or mandate files`
            `the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret` IS `personal data under a professional or official secret`
            `the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number` IS `only name, title and office contact details`
            `the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way` IS `the third party gave an expert opinion`
            `the case is atypical, so that section 5(3) does not settle the weighing` IS `atypical case for section 5(3)`
        `the facts about section 6` MEANS `Facts about section 6` WITH
            `the information contains intellectual property` IS `copyright or other intellectual property`
            `the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access requested` IS `that protection stands in the way`
            `the information contains a trade or business secret` IS `a trade or business secret`
            `the person concerned has consented to access to the trade or business secret` IS `the holder of the secret consented`
        grounds MEANS `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access` WITH
            `facts for section 3 no. 1` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 1`
            `facts for section 3 no. 2` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 2`
            `facts for section 3 no. 3` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 3`
            `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty`
            `facts for section 3 no. 5` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 5`
            `facts for section 3 no. 6` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 6`
            `facts for section 3 no. 7` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 7`
            `facts for section 3 no. 8` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 8`
            `facts for section 4(1)` IS `the facts about section 4(1)`
            `facts for section 5` IS `the facts about section 5`
            `facts for section 6` IS `the facts about section 6`
        request MEANS `Request for a document` WITH
            `is addressed to a federal authority and asks for official information` IS `federal request`
            `the document was prepared outside the Council and the Ministry` IS `prepared outside`
            `the document was submitted to the Council for its deliberations` IS `submitted to the Council`
            `the document is a recommendation an opinion or a closing report of the Council` IS `recommendation or report`
            `another ground for refusing access applies` IS (`a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` grounds)
            `another statutory confidentiality duty attaches to the document` IS `another duty attaches`

@export Which grounds for refusing access under §§ 3 to 6 of the Freedom of Information Act apply to this request for a document of the Expert Advisory Council on Occupational Diseases, if the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV is void because the amending regulation did not cite § 9(1a) sentence 4 of Book VII of the Social Code? Answers with a list of the grounds that apply; an empty list means none does.
GIVEN
    -- the document and the request
    `federal request`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you ask a federal authority, such as the Federal Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs, for official information.
    `prepared outside`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was prepared outside the Expert Advisory Council and the Ministry, for example a statement written by an association; false if it was made inside.
    `submitted to the Council`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document was submitted to the Expert Advisory Council for its deliberations.
    `recommendation or report`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the document is a recommendation, an opinion or a closing report of the Council, the documents § 9(5) sentence 1 BKV makes public.
    `another duty attaches`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a statutory confidentiality duty other than § 9(5) BKV attaches to the document, for example the members' duty of confidentiality; false if none does.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 1
    `harm to international relations`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect Germany's international relations (§ 3 no. 1 a IFG); false if not.
    `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Federal Armed Forces (§ 3 no. 1 b IFG); false if not.
    `harm to internal or external security`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect interests of internal or external security (§ 3 no. 1 c IFG); false if not.
    `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities (§ 3 no. 1 d IFG); false if not.
    `harm to external financial control`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect matters of external financial control (§ 3 no. 1 e IFG); false if not.
    `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade and payments (§ 3 no. 1 f IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a pending court case`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to a fair trial`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect a person's claim to a fair trial (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    `harm to an investigation`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations (§ 3 no. 1 g IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 2
    `danger to public safety`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known could endanger public safety (§ 3 no. 2 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 3
    `impairs confidential international negotiations`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations (§ 3 no. 3 a IFG); false if not.
    `impairs the deliberations of an authority`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known would impair the necessary confidentiality of an authority's deliberations (§ 3 no. 3 b IFG); false if not. Whether a paper that is only a basis for the authority's deliberations and shows nothing of how it formed its view is protected at all was left open in BVerwG 7 C 4.11, para. 32.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty
    `classified as a Verschlusssache`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is classified as a Verschlusssache under the general administrative rule on the protection of classified information (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `professional secret`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a professional secret (Berufsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    `special official secret`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is subject to a special official secret (besonderes Amtsgeheimnis) (§ 3 no. 4 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 5
    `comes from another public body`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information comes from another public body (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if the authority made it.
    `drawn in only temporarily`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority drew the information in only temporarily (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if not.
    `not meant to join its own records`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is not meant to become part of the authority's own records (§ 3 no. 5 IFG); false if it is.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 6
    `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if making the information known is apt to impair the economic interests of the social insurance funds (§ 3 no. 6 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 7
    `received in confidence`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information was collected or transmitted in confidence (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if it was submitted as non-confidential.
    `third party still wants confidence`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, on the day you made the request, the third party who gave the information still had an interest in its being treated as confidential (§ 3 no. 7 IFG); false if that interest has ended.
    -- IFG § 3 no. 8
    `asking an intelligence service`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask is an intelligence service (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    `asking about security-clearance tasks`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the authority you ask performs tasks within § 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act (Sicherheitsüberprüfungsgesetz) and your request concerns those tasks (§ 3 no. 8 IFG); false if not.
    -- IFG § 4(1)
    `a draft of a decision`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a draft of a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `work immediately preparing a decision`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party, such as an association's written statement (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `such a paper still prepares a decision`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual, so that evidence, an expert opinion or a third party's statement does serve the immediate preparation of a decision (§ 4(1) sentence 2 IFG says they regularly do not); false in the usual case.
    `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if, now, making the information known before the decision is taken would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures (§ 4(1) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case, access should still be granted`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that the application should not be refused although § 4(1) IFG would otherwise apply (the provision says it 'should' be refused); false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 5
    `personal data of a third party`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains personal data of a person other than you (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `special category personal data`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation, such as health data (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the third party consented`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person whose data it is has consented to your getting access (§ 5(1) IFG); false if not.
    `the consent was express`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if that consent was given expressly (§ 5(1) sentence 2 IFG); false if there was no consent or it was not express.
    `my interest outweighs the third party interest`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if, weighing your interest in the information against the third party's interest worthy of protection in excluding access, yours outweighs theirs (§ 5(1) sentence 1 IFG). This is a judgment for the authority and then a court: answer it as you expect it to be decided.
    `data from service, office or mandate files`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data come from documents that relate to the third party's service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `personal data under a professional or official secret`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret (§ 5(2) IFG); false if not.
    `only name, title and office contact details`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number (§ 5(3) IFG); false if they go further.
    `the third party gave an expert opinion`                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way (§ 5(3) IFG); false if not.
    `atypical case for section 5(3)`                                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc True only if the case is unusual enough that § 5(3) IFG, which says the interest of the requester outweighs 'in der Regel' (as a rule) in the situation it describes, does not settle the weighing here; false in the usual case.
    -- IFG § 6
    `copyright or other intellectual property`                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains copyright-protected material or other intellectual property (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not.
    `that protection stands in the way`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access you ask for (§ 6 sentence 1 IFG); false if not, for example because the holder of the right agrees.
    `a trade or business secret`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the information contains a trade or business secret (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    `the holder of the secret consented`                                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person concerned, the one whose secret it is, has consented to your getting access to it (§ 6 sentence 2 IFG); false if not.
    -- the citation requirement
    `an exception applies`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if you assume that an exception to the citation requirement applies, so that the 2026 amendment of § 9(5) BKV stands; false assumes none applies and the amendment is void.
GIVETH A LIST OF `Ground for refusing access`
`which grounds for refusing access apply if the 2026 amendment is void` MEANS
    `the grounds for refusing access that apply` (`the reading of section 9(5) BKV to apply` `an exception applies`) request grounds
    WHERE
        `the facts about section 3 no. 1` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 1` WITH
            `disclosure could adversely affect international relations` IS `harm to international relations`
            `disclosure could adversely affect military or other security-sensitive interests of the Bundeswehr` IS `harm to Bundeswehr security interests`
            `disclosure could adversely affect interests of internal or external security` IS `harm to internal or external security`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the control or supervisory tasks of the financial, competition or regulatory authorities` IS `harm to supervision by a financial, competition or regulatory authority`
            `disclosure could adversely affect matters of external financial control` IS `harm to external financial control`
            `disclosure could adversely affect measures to protect against unlawful foreign trade` IS `harm to measures against unlawful foreign trade`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of a pending court case` IS `harm to a pending court case`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the claim of a person to a fair trial` IS `harm to a fair trial`
            `disclosure could adversely affect the conduct of criminal, regulatory-offence or disciplinary investigations` IS `harm to an investigation`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 2` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 2` WITH
            `disclosure could endanger public safety` IS `danger to public safety`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 3` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 3` WITH
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of international negotiations` IS `impairs confidential international negotiations`
            `disclosure would impair the necessary confidentiality of the deliberations of an authority` IS `impairs the deliberations of an authority`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` WITH
            `the information is subject to a duty of secrecy set by the general administrative rule on classified information` IS `classified as a Verschlusssache`
            `the information is subject to a professional secret` IS `professional secret`
            `the information is subject to a special official secret` IS `special official secret`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 5` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 5` WITH
            `the information comes from another public body` IS `comes from another public body`
            `the information was drawn in only temporarily` IS `drawn in only temporarily`
            `the information is not meant to become part of the own records of the authority` IS `not meant to join its own records`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 6` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 6` WITH
            `disclosure is apt to impair fiscal interests of the Federation in commerce` IS `harm to Federal fiscal interests in commerce`
            `disclosure is apt to impair economic interests of the social insurance funds` IS `harm to economic interests of the social insurance funds`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 7` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 7` WITH
            `the information was collected or transmitted in confidence` IS `received in confidence`
            `the interest of the third party in confidential treatment still persists at the time of the request` IS `third party still wants confidence`
        `the facts about section 3 no. 8` MEANS `Facts about section 3 no. 8` WITH
            `the authority asked is an intelligence service` IS `asking an intelligence service`
            `the authority asked performs tasks within section 10 no. 3 of the Security Clearance Act and the information concerns them` IS `asking about security-clearance tasks`
        `the facts about section 4(1)` MEANS `Facts about section 4(1)` WITH
            `the information is a draft of a decision` IS `a draft of a decision`
            `the information is work or a resolution that immediately prepares a decision` IS `work immediately preparing a decision`
            `the information is a result of taking evidence, an expert opinion or a statement of a third party` IS `evidence, expert opinion or third-party statement`
            `a paper of that kind nevertheless serves the immediate preparation of a decision` IS `such a paper still prepares a decision`
            `premature disclosure would frustrate the success of the decision or of imminent official measures` IS `early disclosure would frustrate the decision`
            `the case is atypical, so that the application should not be refused` IS `atypical case, access should still be granted`
        `the facts about section 5` MEANS `Facts about section 5` WITH
            `the information contains personal data of a third party` IS `personal data of a third party`
            `the personal data are of a special category under Article 9(1) of the General Data Protection Regulation` IS `special category personal data`
            `the third party has consented to access` IS `the third party consented`
            `the consent of the third party was express` IS `the consent was express`
            `the interest of the requester in the information outweighs the interest of the third party in excluding access` IS `my interest outweighs the third party interest`
            `the personal data come from documents about the service or office relationship or a mandate of the third party` IS `data from service, office or mandate files`
            `the personal data are subject to a professional or official secret` IS `personal data under a professional or official secret`
            `the personal data are limited to name, title, academic degree, professional or functional designation, office address and office telephone number` IS `only name, title and office contact details`
            `the third party gave an opinion in a proceeding as an expert or in a comparable way` IS `the third party gave an expert opinion`
            `the case is atypical, so that section 5(3) does not settle the weighing` IS `atypical case for section 5(3)`
        `the facts about section 6` MEANS `Facts about section 6` WITH
            `the information contains intellectual property` IS `copyright or other intellectual property`
            `the protection of that intellectual property stands in the way of the access requested` IS `that protection stands in the way`
            `the information contains a trade or business secret` IS `a trade or business secret`
            `the person concerned has consented to access to the trade or business secret` IS `the holder of the secret consented`
        grounds MEANS `Facts bearing on the grounds for refusing access` WITH
            `facts for section 3 no. 1` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 1`
            `facts for section 3 no. 2` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 2`
            `facts for section 3 no. 3` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 3`
            `facts for section 3 no. 4, other than a statutory duty` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 4 other than a statutory duty`
            `facts for section 3 no. 5` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 5`
            `facts for section 3 no. 6` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 6`
            `facts for section 3 no. 7` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 7`
            `facts for section 3 no. 8` IS `the facts about section 3 no. 8`
            `facts for section 4(1)` IS `the facts about section 4(1)`
            `facts for section 5` IS `the facts about section 5`
            `facts for section 6` IS `the facts about section 6`
        request MEANS `Request for a document` WITH
            `is addressed to a federal authority and asks for official information` IS `federal request`
            `the document was prepared outside the Council and the Ministry` IS `prepared outside`
            `the document was submitted to the Council for its deliberations` IS `submitted to the Council`
            `the document is a recommendation an opinion or a closing report of the Council` IS `recommendation or report`
            `another ground for refusing access applies` IS (`a ground for refusal other than a statutory duty applies` grounds)
            `another statutory confidentiality duty attaches to the document` IS `another duty attaches`
